# Trivy ignore list — CONTAINER IMAGE scan only.
#
# Deliberately separate from `.trivyignore`, which governs the filesystem scan
# of this repository's own dependency tree. The two scan different things and
# must not share suppressions: a CVE that is unfixable inside a vendored
# third-party binary is not the same as one in our lockfile, and suppressing it
# in the shared file would switch off the regression detection the filesystem
# gate exists to provide.
#
# CVE-2026-69152 below is the sharp edge that makes the split necessary: it was
# genuinely FIXED in our lockfile (#773), so it must keep failing the
# filesystem scan if it ever regresses — while the copy vendored inside pnpm's
# binary is beyond our reach.
#
# Every entry here needs an `SD-*` rationale, same rule as the other file.

# SD-23: three HIGH findings vendored INSIDE the pnpm distribution that ships in
# the backend runtime image. They live in corepack's cached pnpm tree, so
# `pnpm.overrides` cannot reach them and neither can a lockfile change.
#
# pnpm is required at runtime: `scripts/railway-start.js` boots the server with
# `pnpm exec medusa start` and runs migrations with
# `pnpm exec medusa db:migrate --execute-safe-links`. It therefore cannot be
# removed the way npm was — npm IS removed from both node runtime images, and
# that is what cleared most of the image findings.
#
# pnpm was bumped 10.13.1 -> 10.34.5 here, taking the backend image from 51
# HIGH/CRITICAL to 4. The remaining three need pnpm 11.x:
#
#   CVE-2026-69152  brace-expansion 2.1.2  fixed in 2.1.4
#   CVE-2026-69192  ip-address 10.2.0      fixed in 10.3.1
#   CVE-2026-55697  pnpm 10.34.5           fixed in 11.5.3
#
# pnpm 11 is a package-manager major: it moves the `packageManager` pin for
# every workspace, CI and local dev, and needs its own lockfile-compatibility
# pass. Tracked as a separate workstream rather than smuggled into a CVE fix.
#
# CVE-2026-14257 also applies to this vendored copy and is already suppressed
# in `.trivyignore` under SD-22 for the same unfixable function-export line;
# repeated here because the two files do not share entries.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
CVE-2026-69192
CVE-2026-55697
